---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Jack Yu | Physics at Caltech">
  <div class="intro-grid">
    <section class="home-intro" aria-labelledby="home-title">
      <h1 id="home-title">About Me</h1>
      <p>
        I'm a sophomore physics major at Caltech. Very vaguely, I'm interested
        in building instrumentation / experimental setups for things
        <sup>
          <a
            id="about-footnote-ref"
            href="#about-footnote"
            aria-label="Jump to footnote"
          >
            1
          </a>
        </sup>{" "}
        that solve interesting problems.
      </p>
    </section>

    <div class="home-media">
      <picture>
        <source srcset="/images/headshot.avif" type="image/avif" />
        <source srcset="/images/headshot.webp" type="image/webp" />
        <img
          class="headshot"
          src="/images/headshotcompressed.jpg"
          alt="Portrait of Jack Yu"
          width="682"
          height="910"
          fetchpriority="high"
        />
      </picture>
    </div>
    <aside class="footnote" id="about-footnote" aria-label="Footnote">
      <p>
        <sup>1</sup> Recently: quantum computing / sensing, energy storage,
        atomic clocks, various types of cool microscopy and spectroscopy, etc.{" "}
        <a
          class="footnote-back"
          href="#about-footnote-ref"
          aria-label="Back to sentence"
        >
          ↩
        </a>
      </p>
    </aside>
  </div>

  <section class="home-copy" aria-label="About Jack">
    <p>
      At Caltech, I work with Professor Rana Adhikari's{" "}
      <a href="https://caltechexperimentalgravity.github.io/">
        Experimental Gravity Group
      </a>
      , modeling photonic quantum states for applications in quantum computing
      and precision sensing at LIGO. . In the{" "}
      <a href="https://cushinglab.caltech.edu/">Cushing Lab</a>, I work on
      instrumentation for studying ionic motion in solid-state electrolytes.
    </p>
    <p>
      Before Caltech, I spent two summers in optoelectronics R&D at Sandia
      National Laboratories, working on lasers, optical characterization, and
      experimental hardware.
    </p>
    <p>
      Outside the lab, I swim on Caltech's NCAA team, make prints, take
      photographs, and read science fiction.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
